  "legenda": "This Sunday, Bangladesh: Craft, Culture & Hope at the World Hope Forum\nSign Up for FREE @worldhopeforum\n\nMeet the speaker: \nMahenaz Chowdury is a cultural researcher, curator and conscious designer known for her decolonial approach to craft and cultural preservation. Founder of Broqué and workshop lead at Dhaka Makers, she uses artisanal knowledge as a tool for collaboration and social change. Her projects — including Once There Were Rivers, Loomscape and Weaving Continuity — explore Bangladeshi craft, Jamdani textiles and community resilience in the face of displacement, urbanisation and climate change.\n\nSunday, January 25, 2026\n19:00-22:00 Dhaka BST\n14:00-17:00 Paris CET\n8:00-11:00 New York EST\n\nphoto 3: @pobitroduniya\nphoto 5: @faiza_noon",
  "legenda_completa": "This Sunday, Bangladesh: Craft, Culture & Hope at the World Hope Forum\nSign Up for FREE @worldhopeforum\n\nMeet the speaker: \nMahenaz Chowdury is a cultural researcher, curator and conscious designer known for her decolonial approach to craft and cultural preservation. Founder of Broqué and workshop lead at Dhaka Makers, she uses artisanal knowledge as a tool for collaboration and social change. Her projects — including Once There Were Rivers, Loomscape and Weaving Continuity — explore Bangladeshi craft, Jamdani textiles and community resilience in the face of displacement, urbanisation and climate change.\n\nSunday, January 25, 2026\n19:00-22:00 Dhaka BST\n14:00-17:00 Paris CET\n8:00-11:00 New York EST\n\nphoto 3: @pobitroduniya\nphoto 5: @faiza_noon",
